## Summary

**Implemented** `crates/application/src/transfer.rs` (1061 lines) — the resumable download worker.

**§8.4 state machine** — `DownloadJobState` enum with all 8 variants (serde `snake_case`); `transition()` validates each edge against the diagram and rejects everything else as `StateTransitionError::Invalid` (no silent corrections). `can_transition_to` / `allowed_targets` / `is_terminal` helpers; `initial()` is `Planned`.

**§8.5 transfer limits** — chunk planning via `plan_chunks(total, mode)` using `TRANSFER_CHUNK_BYTES`; backoff via `backoff_delay_ms(attempt)` using base/max constants; `max_parallel_chunks_for(platform_label)` for the android/desktop split.

**Resumability** — `DownloadJobStore` trait abstracts the `download_jobs` persistence boundary (A-02 indirection — concrete impl will live in `storage-sqlite`). On `resume`, each chunk marked `verified` is re-read and its bytes re-hashed; only chunks whose recorded digest matches recomputed sha256 are skipped, all others are re-fetched. Writes are streaming (no full chunk held in memory).

**`DownloadWorker`** — `start`/`resume`/`pause`/`fail` plus `approve_full_transfer` (the §8.5 user-approved bounded-full-transfer fallback when the provider returns `InvalidRangeResponse` or `RangeUnsupported`) and `begin_activation`/`complete_activation` for the install layer (`install_transactions`-owned edge).

**Bounded parallelism** — `tokio::sync::Semaphore` + `JoinSet` over `Arc<dyn DownloadJobStore>`; first hard failure aborts the batch and transitions `Fetching → Failed`.

**`cargo check -p application`**: **0 errors and 0 warnings in `transfer.rs`**. The build is blocked solely by 12 pre-existing errors in `ports/src/platform.rs` (5 undefined platform types — another task; explicitly excluded by the task spec) and one `domain/src/annotation.rs` unused-import warning.
